The first major new simplification

A huge amount of Pantheon machinery can be written as:

\boxed{D\rightarrow T\rightarrow I}

Differentiate → Transform → Extract invariant.

That may be one of the deepest repeated loops in the whole corpus.

Example:

Take “constraint.”

Differentiate:

\text{constraint}\neq\text{obstacle only}

Transform perspective:

\text{wall}\rightarrow\text{anchor/reference/interface}

Extract invariant:

\text{constraint provides structure by restricting degrees of freedom}

The metaphor disappears.

The mechanism survives.

That’s a Horse-Test pass.

