Second family: the learning machinery

Several other Pantheon mechanisms collapse into a different loop.

Ouroboros with Metabolism, Kintsugi, Compound Delta Engine, fail-forward-fast, Afterglow, Metamap learning, Fitness Route.

Strip the names and I get:

x_t
\rightarrow
a_t
\rightarrow
o_t
\rightarrow
\Delta_t
\rightarrow
u(\Delta_t)
\rightarrow
x_{t+1}

The underlying horse is:

\boxed{\text{Act → Observe → Extract useful error → Update}}

Call the primitive:

\boxed{M=\text{Metabolize Delta}}

Now something interesting happens.

Ouroboros is not the primitive.

Recursion is merely the topology.

The actual capability comes from:

\boxed{\text{recursion}+\text{selective update}}

So I would demote raw recursion from “mechanism” to routing structure.

That’s a useful cleanup.

