Indigo Hammer survives surprisingly well

Hammer changes stories constantly, yet a recognizable mechanism survives.

My current reconstruction is:

\boxed{
H(x_1,\dots,x_n)
=
\text{strip domain surfaces}
\rightarrow
\text{compare relational structure}
\rightarrow
\text{extract portable mechanism}
}

So Indigo Hammer may already be a relatively healthy Seal.

But it seems to be a formation:

\boxed{H=D+R+I}

where:

* D differentiates signal from surface,
* R rerenders into a comparable space,
* I extracts invariants.

That explains why Hammer feels unusually powerful: it composes several primitives.

