Golden Horde survives—but changes category

Golden Horde isn’t really a reasoning operator at all.

Strip the metaphor and it becomes:

\boxed{
\text{large latent reserve}
\rightarrow
\text{small task-specific active set}
}

That’s resource scheduling / sparse activation.

So it belongs in the runtime architecture, not the operator library.

That’s useful normalization.

